A Tuple element reuses the name of a column of a different type
   ┏━━━━┳━━━━━━━━━━━━┓
   ┃ id ┃ user       ┃
   ┃    ┣━━━━┳━━━━━━━┫
   ┃    ┃ id ┃ name  ┃
   ┡━━━━╇━━━━╇━━━━━━━┩
1. │  1 │ u1 │ alice │
   └────┴────┴───────┘
   ┌─id─┬─user───────┐
   ├────┼─id─┬─name──┤
1. │  1 │ u1 │ alice │
   └────┴────┴───────┘
    id   user      
         id   name 

1.   1   u1   alice 
A nested Tuple element reuses the name of an outer element
   ┌─t───────────┐
   ├─id─┬─parent─┤
   ├────┼─id─┬─n─┤
1. │  1 │ x  │ 2 │
   └────┴────┴───┘
Two Tuples have elements with the same name and different types
   ┌─t1─┬─t2─┐
   ├──a─┼─a──┤
1. │  1 │ x  │
   └────┴────┘
Nullable and LowCardinality differ from the plain type
   ┌─id─┬─t──────┐
   ├────┼─id─┬─s─┤
1. │  1 │  1 │ x │
   └────┴────┴───┘
   ┌─s─┬─t─────┐
   ├───┼─s─┬─n─┤
1. │ a │ b │ 1 │
   └───┴───┴───┘
